## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates multi-tenant isolation, model versioning, and controlled rollout in real-time inference.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker endpoint variants and traffic shifting
- SageMaker Model Registry and Pipelines for versioning
- Tenant-level routing and isolation, least-privilege IAM, PrivateLink
- Drift detection with SageMaker Clarify and per-tenant monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for per-tenant routing in the inference container
function route(event){
  const tenant = event.tenant_id;
  const variant = tenantVariantMap[tenant] || 'prod';
  // forward to the corresponding variant
  return invokeVariant(variant, event.payload);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rollback safety across tenants during a failed canary?
- How would you model per-tenant cost and scale limits in DynamoDB and CloudWatch?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of explainability and governance as essential components of production ML workflows, not just model performance.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Clarify for feature attributions and bias detection
- Model Registry and Pipelines for full traceability and lineage
- Lightweight dashboards (QuickSight) for non-technical stakeholders
- Drift detection and automated rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Call SageMaker Clarify for per-inference feature attributions
const explanation = await clarify.explain({
  model: 'sentiment-classifier-v1',
  data: { text: 'This product is amazing!' }
});

// Retrieve bias score
const biasReport = await clarify.getBiasScore({
  model: 'sentiment-classifier-v1',
  dataset: 'production-reviews'
});

// Register model with explanations
await modelRegistry.register({
  modelName: 'sentiment-classifier-v1',
  explanations: explanation,
  biasScore: biasReport
});
```
